  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "In Mexico, the hotel brands **commonly considered** for branded residences include **Four Seasons, Ritz-Carlton, St. Regis, Rosewood, Aman, Auberge, Montage, Viceroy, Hyatt brands such as Thompson, Park Hyatt, and Kimpton, plus Waldorf Astoria, Hilton, Fairmont, Banyan Tree, SLS, Mondrian, MGallery, and Accor-linked brands like Hyde and Faena**.[1][2][4][5][6][7][9][10][13][16][17]\n\nThe strongest recurring names across the Mexico-focused sources are **Four Seasons, Ritz-Carlton, St. Regis, Rosewood, Auberge, Montage, and Hyatt-affiliated brands** such as **Thompson** and **Kimpton**.[1][2][4][5][6][10][15][19][20]\n\nA practical way to think about the market is by brand family:\n- **Marriott / Ritz-Carlton / St. Regis**: frequently cited in Mexico luxury-branded projects.[1][2][6][10][20]\n- **Four Seasons / Park Hyatt / Thompson / Kimpton / Waldorf Astoria / Conrad / Hilton**: all appear in Mexico branded-residence or hotel-residence developments.[1][3][4][7][8][10][13]\n- **Independent luxury brands**: **Rosewood, Aman, Auberge, Montage, Viceroy, Banyan Tree, Chablé, Faena**.[1][4][5][6][10][12][16][19]\n- **Lifestyle / design-led brands**: **SLS, Mondrian, MGallery, Hyde, W Hotels, The Standard**.[1][2][9][13][16]\n\nIf you want, I can also narrow this to the **most active brands in Los Cabos, Riviera Maya, Punta Mita, or Mexico City**.",
